<title>NETHERLANDS: ASM INTERNATIONAL WINS QPL ORDER.</title>
<headline>ASM INTERNATIONAL WINS QPL ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Semiconductor equipment maker ASM International NV said on Wednesday it had won a &quot;multi million dollar order&quot; from British semiconductor maker Newport Wafer-Fab Limited (NWL).</p>
<p>NWL, a unit of Hong Kong's QPL International, has ordered four of ASM International's Advance 400 systems for its new Fab 3 facility in the town of Newport, to be delivered in the fourth quarter of this year.</p>
<p>The Fab 3 plant will manufacture microchips on eight inch silicon wafers using deep submicron technology and will be expanded to a capacity of 10,000 or more wafers per month.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
